# Sending Welcome Emails

Here's a clean implementation with a few variations depending on your needs.

## Basic Sequential Version

```javascript
/**
 * Sends a welcome email to each user in the list.
 * @param {Array} users - Array of user objects.
 * @param {Function} sendEmail - Async function that sends an email to a user.
 */
async function sendWelcomeEmails(users, sendEmail) {
  for (const user of users) {
    await sendEmail(user);
  }
}
```

**Why sequential?** If your email provider has rate limits or you want to avoid overwhelming the service, sending one at a time is safest.

## Parallel Version (Faster)

```javascript
async function sendWelcomeEmails(users, sendEmail) {
  await Promise.all(users.map(user => sendEmail(user)));
}
```

This fires all emails at once — fast, but risky if the API has rate limits.

## Robust Version (Recommended)

This version handles failures gracefully and optionally limits concurrency:

```javascript
async function sendWelcomeEmails(users, sendEmail, { concurrency = 5 } = {}) {
  const results = { sent: [], failed: [] };

  // Process users in batches of `concurrency`
  for (let i = 0; i < users.length; i += concurrency) {
    const batch = users.slice(i, i + concurrency);

    const settled = await Promise.allSettled(
      batch.map(user => sendEmail(user).then(() => user))
    );

    for (const outcome of settled) {
      if (outcome.status === 'fulfilled') {
        results.sent.push(outcome.value);
      } else {
        results.failed.push({ error: outcome.reason });
      }
    }
  }

  return results;
}
```

## Usage Example

```javascript
const users = [
  { name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
  { name: 'Bob',   email: 'bob@example.com'   },
  { name: 'Carol', email: 'carol@example.com' },
];

// Mock sendEmail
async function sendEmail(user) {
  console.log(`Sending welcome email to ${user.email}...`);
  // await someEmailAPI.send(user.email, 'Welcome!');
}

const { sent, failed } = await sendWelcomeEmails(users, sendEmail);
console.log(`Sent: ${sent.length}, Failed: ${failed.length}`);
```

## Key Considerations

| Approach | Speed | Safety | Best For |
|----------|-------|--------|----------|
| Sequential | Slow | ✅ Safe | Rate-limited APIs, small lists |
| `Promise.all` | Fast | ⚠️ Risky | Small lists, high-throughput APIs |
| Batched | Balanced | ✅ Safe | Production use, large lists |

**Important:** `Promise.all` rejects on the *first* failure, abandoning the rest. `Promise.allSettled` (used in the batched version) lets every email attempt complete and reports which ones failed — essential when you need a reliable send log.

