}

const stats = await sendWelcomeEmails(users, sendEmail);
console.log(stats); // { sent: 2, failed: 0 }
```

## Key Design Choices

| Choice | Why |
|---|---|
| `Promise.allSettled` | One failure doesn't abort the whole batch |
| Sequential loop (v1) | Simplest; respects ordering; good for small lists |
| Parallel (v2) | Much faster for large lists |
| Batching (v3) | Avoids hitting provider rate limits or overwhelming the SMTP server |
| Returning stats | Caller can log, retry, or alert on failures |

Pick the version that matches your list size and provider constraints. For a handful of users, the basic version is fine; for hundreds or thousands, use the batched version.

